NUM-04: divide SI snow melt coefficients by 1.8 instead of multiplying

setMeltParams() converted the [SNOWPACKS] melt coefficients Cmin/Cmax from
mm/hr per deg C to ft/sec per deg F with x * UCF(TEMPERATURE) / UCF(RAINFALL).
A coefficient per deg C is 1.8 times the same coefficient per deg F, so the
SI value must be divided by UCF(TEMPERATURE) = 1.8, not multiplied. SI packs
melted 3.24 times faster than specified. US models are unchanged
(UCF(TEMPERATURE) = 1).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-04_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/snow.c b/src/legacy/engine/snow.c
index d415675..e9d7d1d 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/snow.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/snow.c
@@ -328,8 +328,9 @@ void setMeltParams(int j, int k, double x[])
     if ( k >= SNOW_PLOWABLE && k <= SNOW_PERV )
     {
         // --- min/max melt coeffs.
-        Snowmelt[j].dhmin[k]     = x[0] * UCF(TEMPERATURE) / UCF(RAINFALL);
-        Snowmelt[j].dhmax[k]     = x[1] * UCF(TEMPERATURE) / UCF(RAINFALL); 
+        //     (a coefficient per deg C is 1.8 times one per deg F)
+        Snowmelt[j].dhmin[k]     = x[0] / UCF(TEMPERATURE) / UCF(RAINFALL);
+        Snowmelt[j].dhmax[k]     = x[1] / UCF(TEMPERATURE) / UCF(RAINFALL); 
 
         // --- base melt temp (deg F)
         Snowmelt[j].tbase[k]     = x[2];
